# XCU 1.7 Intrinsic Utilities
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The intrinsic utilities are found without a search of PATH.

assertion  XCU.1.7-intrinsic-utilities.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.7/search during command search and execution
class      required
since      1992
says       When PATH names a directory holding executable files named alias, cd,
           command, getopts, hash, kill, read, type, ulimit, umask, unalias and
           wait, invoking each of those names as a simple
           command in the shell does not run the file.
timeout    60
test       t/001-no-path-search.sh

assertion  XCU.1.7-intrinsic-utilities.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.7/Intrinsic Utilities
class      required
since      1992
says       With PATH naming only an empty directory, type and command -v still
           find each of the twelve intrinsic utilities that are not part of the
           User Portability Utilities option (alias, cd, command, getopts, hash,
           kill, read, type, ulimit, umask, unalias, wait).
timeout    60
test       t/002-found-with-empty-path.sh

assertion  XCU.1.7-intrinsic-utilities.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.7/Intrinsic Utilities
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       The intrinsic utilities bg, fc, fg and jobs are found without a PATH
           search: invoking them with PATH naming a directory of files of those
           names does not run the files, and type and command -v find them when
           PATH names only an empty directory.
timeout    60
test       t/003-up-intrinsic.sh
